WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.168
♪ (SOMBER MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.003
STEPHEN PANDOS:
 This is Jennifer's note.

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:06.923
JENNIFER PANDOS: I can't erase
 the things I've done.

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:09.759
There is no place left to run.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.763
Life is hard, but it goes on.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:17.642
Live my days
as if they were my last.

00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.728
(SCHOOL BELL RINGS)

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:24.274
STEPHEN: Jennifer Pandos
 was reported missing in 1987.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.693
SPEAKER: Never been seen
 or heard from since.

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:28.278
STEPHEN: I'm Jennifer's brother.

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.779
I reached out to an attorney

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.407
about whether
I could sue my parents

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.493
for the death of my sister.

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.289
For the first 22 years
of her disappearance,

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.292
everything I'd been told,
you know, was a lie.

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:45.754
I thought, at first,
she had run away

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:47.005
and that she didn't tell me.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.131
And it's like,
who is this person?

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.049
STEPHEN: I think my mother
 knows what happened.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.552
You waited two days
to call the police?

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:54.929
My father scared her
to keep this a secret.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:57.265
-So, you really think I did it?
-STEPHEN: (OVER PHONE) Yes.

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.602
SPEAKER 2:
 They both failed polygraphs.

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:01.936
I wanna know the truth.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:05.565
I cannot tell you something
I don't know.

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:08.568
STEPHEN: The story around
 Jennifer's disappearance,

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:09.944
it doesn't make sense.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.530
It feels like
you've convicted me

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:14.657
of something
that I haven't done.

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:16.951
SPEAKER 3: This must be
 very emotional for you.

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:19.662
My heart is racing
a mile a minute.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.082
Everybody has that case

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.044
that impacted them
more than any other.

00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:30.298
STEPHEN: The shame of thinking
 my parents were involved.

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:33.176
SPEAKER: It's made him
 question everything.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.637
SPEAKER 4: Why are you
 so consumed about this?

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.389
Because it's only right,
and she deserves better.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.475
-You think it's crazy...
-(KNOCKING)

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:42.727
...and then, all of a sudden,
it's even more crazy.

00:01:45.355 --> 00:01:46.856
I'll never give up on Jennifer.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.483
I just have to keep on going.

